"1ekm8nr448g": "When letter (4) arrived on August 19, the detective bureau sent every letter received so far under the Hourglass name to the crime lab, eleven in all, counting the ones sent to other papers and to the sheriff's office.",
"1h9cqbia7up": "Two references: letters (1) and (2), the pair the bureau filed together as one writer's from the start. Of the rest, four were still in the running at the end. The lab attributes only one of those to the same writer.",
"1qdqlyx6qsd": "Reference — letter (1), received Dec 17 · letter (2), received May 6",
"4x3ktxbcl0": "Blue ballpoint capitals. Both have THE SAND RUNS as the first line. Sheet folded three times across, then bent once more lengthwise — the envelope bulges. Stamp at upper right, upside down. Postmarked at post offices in towns north of the bay, Monday-morning pickup.",
"1iaetccdklv": "Which letter can be attributed to the same writer?",
"hcqlc5u6me": "Letter (3) · May 9 · to the Courier",
"1ca37wasmgd": "Typed. No THE SAND RUNS on the first line. Gives the victim's name as “Ann Norris.” Folded twice. Stamp straight. Postmarked Knowlton main post office, Thursday afternoon.",
"1ixgctopdov": "To the Evening Star · May 13",
"2192euh8mdr": "Blue ballpoint capitals. First line THE SAND IS RUNNING. Folded three times, bent once. Stamp straight. Postmarked Knowlton main post office, Monday afternoon. Several sentences lifted word for word from the Courier's May 9 front page.",
"11jretvtgeg": "Letter (4) · Aug 19 · to the Courier",
"29t8u1fp1ze": "Blue ballpoint capitals. First line THE SAND RUNS. Folded three times, bent once. Stamp at upper right, upside down. Postmarked Port Haley post office, Monday-morning pickup.",
"nhfhiyhw4l": "To the Sheriff's Office · June 4",
"1tv2ulwve0m": "Pencil capitals. No first line. Says the radio in the Mason Hill car was on. Folded three times. Stamp at upper right, upside down. Postmarked Santa Reina post office, Tuesday afternoon.",
"1d71xhelb9a": "The first line existed only inside the cipher, and its solution never ran in the paper. Anyone who listened to the police radio knew about the car radio.",
"3yk6zpxjz6": "Lab reply — letter (4) is attributed to the same writer as (1) and (2). First line, fold marks and upside-down stamp all match. Each of the other three fails on at least one of these.",
"183tql80yjp": "Three envelopes from the same writer — Santa Reina, Dec 16; Millbrook, May 5; Port Haley, Aug 18. All three are Monday-morning pickups: each went into that town's mailbox after the last Saturday-afternoon collection and before the first Monday collection. All three post offices replied — each town has just one public mailbox, [[the mailbox in front of the post office|k_dawnbox]].",
"23g45i6pahb": "Lab memo: in all three, a single sheet was folded three times, bent once more, and pushed in while still thicker than the envelope's mouth. On all three envelopes, both corners of the opening are stretched.",
